  triage:highestOpenBranch "feature/pAI-s16-offline-reconciliation" ;
  triage:correctionNote "2026-07-27 (quality-mgr): arch-ctm recommended closing this as disproven by current code/docs. Independently re-verified against integrate/phase-AI@f3b6a77a: crates/atm-daemon/src/local_ipc_transport.rs still binds and serves BOTH the UDS LocalSocketListener and #[cfg(unix)] tcp_loopback: LocalTcpLoopbackServer concurrently (bind_after_install line 271, serve_runtime_scope line 404). Confirmed no production client anywhere connects via UDS: find crates -name '*.rs' | xargs grep -ln LocalSocketStream matches only server/test-only files (test_support.rs, local_ipc_transport.rs + submodules, local_ipc_wake.rs); the sole production client connection code, crates/atm-core/src/graft.rs:302,564, uses TcpStream::connect/connect_timeout exclusively, an intentional permanent migration per commit 88e8c784. Note: the s11 occurrence below was previously closed on the reasoning that 'concurrent UDS+TCP binding is REQUIRED per REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-001, not dead infra' -- that reasoning answers a different question than the one this finding actually raises. REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-001 does require the UDS listener to exist server-side; it says nothing about whether any client reaches it, and none currently does. The finding's real claim (dead/unreferenced-by-any-client production infrastructure kept alive) is CONFIRMED true, not disproven. Top-level status was never closed and remains correct as-is. Declining arch-ctm's batch-close recommendation for this finding and its AI11 pair (identical defect, see AI11-QA5-RBQA-F001.ttl)." ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-22T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

